  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{2}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{2}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/8974b1f9f7fe7b9b2a8ce2981bfcac086114802c8a025cd3760a9f1d73728d90.png)",
